# WhatsApp Business / Meta Cloud API

## Architecture
- One `whatsapp` module: `webhook.controller` (receive), `whatsapp.service` (send), `templates.service`,
  `conversations.service`, BullMQ queues `wa-inbound` and `wa-outbound`.
- Multi-tenant: each tenant maps to its own WABA ID + phone_number_id(s) + access token, stored encrypted.
  Tenant is resolved from `phone_number_id` in the webhook payload — never trust a tenant id from the body.
- Onboarding of client numbers through **Embedded Signup** (Spacode as Tech Provider). Store the
  business token exchange result securely; never log it.
- Pin the Graph API version in config (e.g. `META_GRAPH_VERSION`), upgrade deliberately with an ADR.

## Webhooks
- `GET` verification: compare `hub.verify_token` with the env secret, echo `hub.challenge`.
- `POST`: verify `X-Hub-Signature-256` (HMAC-SHA256 of the **raw body** with the app secret) before anything else.
- Return `200` within a few seconds; push the payload to `wa-inbound` and process async.
- Deduplicate by `messages[].id` / `statuses[].id` (Meta retries). Store raw payloads (JSONB) for debugging with retention limits.
- Handle statuses: `sent`, `delivered`, `read`, `failed` (store error code/title).

## Messaging rules
- **24-hour customer service window**: free-form messages only within 24h of the user's last inbound
  message. Outside it, only **approved templates**.
- Templates are defined in code/DB with name, language (`he`), category (MARKETING / UTILITY /
  AUTHENTICATION), variables and example values; synced with Meta and their approval status tracked.
- Marketing templates require recorded opt-in; honor opt-out keywords (e.g. "הסר", "STOP") immediately.
- Respect messaging limits / quality rating per number; outbound sends go through the queue with rate limiting
  and back-off on error codes (e.g. 131048/131056 rate/spam limits, 130429 throughput).
- Phone numbers stored in E.164 (`9725XXXXXXXX`), normalized on input.

## Tokens & assets
- Use **System User** tokens (non-expiring or long-lived) for server calls, never personal user tokens.
- Monitor token validity and webhook subscription health; alert on failure.
- Separate Meta app / test number for develop and staging. Never send from the production number in tests.

## Every system gets an official WhatsApp channel
Connected officially through Meta (Cloud API, Embedded Signup — never unofficial libraries/WhatsApp Web
automation, which risk bans). It serves four functions, all logged to the CRM:
1. **Customer service** — the system's AI customer-service agent answers, with human hand-off.
2. **Lead generation** — click-to-WhatsApp ads, website/landing buttons, QR codes; every entry point carries a
   source tag (`ref`/prefilled text/UTM) so the lead is created with its source.
3. **Lead warming (nurturing)** — sequences of approved templates + in-window messages, triggered by lead stage
   and behavior, with frequency caps, quiet hours (no sends on Shabbat/holidays or late night unless the client
   decides otherwise) and immediate stop on reply or opt-out.
4. **Lead assignment** — routing rules by **group** (product, region, language, segment) and **source**
   (campaign, channel, landing page); round-robin or weighted within a group; SLA timer and re-assignment if no response.
Implementation: skill `whatsapp-lead-engine`.

## Bots & AI on WhatsApp
- Bot flows are state machines persisted per conversation (state, context, last_inbound_at).
- Always offer a path to a human agent; hand-off pauses the bot for that conversation.
- AI replies follow the AI-agent rules (guardrails, cost limits, no PII leakage to logs).
